I must assume that, WRT pre-selection of roles, there are different
types of players, for example...
- players that start with a role they feel to be easy because they
   don't die very often in the first few levels (like Valkyries and
   Barbarians),
- players that select roles because of their interest in the class
   (you named it Monk-and-Ninja disease?, but also Wizards are very
   popular RPG classes, and there are also people that select the
   somewhat "strange" classes like Tourists just out of interest),
- players that play Nethack for a long time and want to play a new
   available class (like the Monk and Ranger that haven't been part
   of Nethack in earlier versions),
- players that just select the classes they haven't yet ascended,
- players that select classes randomly, whether they ascended or not.
All these selection habits have been cultivated in different phases
of just _my_ Nethack life, so there may even be more unknown to me.

The pre-selection process influences the possible conclusions one can
draw.[*]

Your introduced selection of data on ascenders seems to me to conceal
the fact that the underlying problem of the selection isn't solved.

